I fixed the bug in `frontend/app/properties/PropertiesClient.tsx`. Each search on the page now gets an increasing request number, kept in a ref. When a response arrives, it only updates the list, the total and the loading spinner if it belongs to the newest request; responses from older searches are ignored. A slow request for the earlier term can no longer overwrite the newer results, whichever finishes first.

The type check passes for this file. There are no existing tests for this page, so I haven't run the change against a real slow response. I didn't touch any tests or the API layer.

One small thing remains: if the old response arrives during the 300 ms delay before the new search is sent, the old results can show for a moment. The new results then replace them, so the list doesn't stay wrong.
